401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Before developing the VacciCare+ Child Vaccination Management System, a feasibility study was conducted to ensure that the proposed solution is practical, achievable, and beneficial. The study covers the following aspects:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1.Operational Feasibility : The system is designed to be user-friendly for parents, hospitals, and administrators. Parents can easily register, book appointments, and receive reminders. Hospitals can manage appointments and update vaccination status, while administrators oversee data and approvals. Since all stakeholders benefit directly, operational feasibility is strong.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (2. Economic Feasibility :  The system reduces dependence on paper-based records and manual tracking, lowering administrative costs for healthcare providers. Since the project relies on open-source tools, development costs are minimal. The long-term benefits of timely vaccination and reduced disease risk far outweigh the development and maintenance expenses.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (3. Legal Feasibility : The system ensures secure handling of child and parent data, complying with privacy and ethical standards. Sensitive data is stored securely in the database, and access is restricted to authorized users only \(parents, hospitals, admin\). )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4.Social Feasibility : Parents and healthcare workers face difficulties in managing vaccination records manually. A digital system that sends reminders, ensures timely vaccination, and simplifies record access is likely to be well-accepted by users. This enhances trust in healthcare and contributes to improved child health outcomes.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
